---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const description="Launch an underwater environmental sensor fleet. Compare provisioned stations, local vacancy repair, and bounded assistance through the same unreliable acoustic mesh.";
const path='/intelligence/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'LearningResource',name:"Ocean Swarm",description,url:'https://iamrobin.ai'+path,learningResourceType:'Interactive simulation',inLanguage:'en'};
const content="<div class=\"swarm-lab\"><a class=\"lab-back\" href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/\">← Agent Swarm Lab</a><p class=\"lab-kicker\">Field study 05 / 06 · Ocean Swarm</p><header class=\"lab-head\"><h1>The sea moves.<br><em>The plan must too.</em></h1><p class=\"lab-deck\">A surface mothership releases a constellation of environmental sensors. The children meet currents, uncertainty, delay—and silence.</p></header><p class=\"lab-zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">海在移动，计划也必须移动。</p><section class=\"lab-stage\" data-swarm-model=\"/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/\" aria-label=\"Ocean Swarm interactive simulator\">\n <div class=\"lab-stage-top\"><span><i class=\"lab-live-dot\"></i>OBSERVATORY / 05</span><span>Seeded simulation · evaluator view</span></div>\n <div class=\"lab-grid\"><div class=\"lab-view\"><canvas class=\"lab-world\" data-world aria-label=\"Animated orthographic 3D sketch of simulator states. Current and final measures are available in the table below.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-camera\"><button type=\"button\" data-camera>Plan / 3D</button><button type=\"button\" data-rotate>Rotate ↻</button></div></div>\n <aside class=\"lab-side\"><label>Treatment<select data-arm aria-label=\"Treatment\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-readout\"><strong data-live-value>—</strong><span data-live-label>Station uptime</span></div><p class=\"lab-event\" data-event>Observe. Compare. Change one assumption.</p><p class=\"small\">Lit site = covered · dim site = uncovered · cross = failed body.</p><div class=\"lab-checks\"><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-compare/>Compare all</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-trails checked/>Trails</label><label><input type=\"checkbox\" data-signals checked/>Links</label></div><label>Inspect a body<select data-agent aria-label=\"Agent to inspect\"></select></label><div class=\"lab-inspect\" data-inspect><p class=\"small\">Click a body in the world, or choose it here. This is an evaluator view of recorded state.</p></div></aside></div>\n <div class=\"lab-buttons\"><button class=\"primary\" type=\"button\" data-play aria-pressed=\"false\">Play world</button><button type=\"button\" data-replay>Replay ↺</button><button type=\"button\" data-end>Final tick →</button><button type=\"button\" data-next-seed>Next seed</button><button type=\"button\" data-download>Save this run ↓</button></div>\n <label class=\"lab-timeline\"><span class=\"tiny\">Time</span><input data-timeline aria-label=\"Simulation timeline\" type=\"range\" min=\"0\" max=\"100\" value=\"0\"/><output data-time>0 ticks</output></label>\n <p class=\"lab-status\" data-status role=\"status\">Loading the model. Recorded evidence remains available below.</p>\n <div class=\"lab-controls\"><div><label>Choose a world<select data-preset aria-label=\"World preset\"></select></label><p data-preset-note></p><button type=\"button\" data-apply>Run these parameters →</button></div><form class=\"lab-params\" data-params aria-label=\"World parameters\"></form></div>\n <div class=\"lab-scores\"><p class=\"tiny\">Station uptime / % · higher is better</p><canvas data-curve class=\"lab-curve\" aria-label=\"Measured outcome over time for each treatment. Dashed markers identify interventions.\"></canvas><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><thead><tr><th>Treatment</th><th>At this tick</th><th>At mission end</th></tr></thead><tbody data-scores></tbody></table></div></div>\n <noscript><p>JavaScript is needed to run the simulator. Read the saved multi-seed evidence and method below.</p></noscript>\n </section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">01 / Try to break it</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Take away the mother. Keep watching the children.</h2><p>Begin with an ordinary deployment. Lose several children, then break acoustic communication, then choose the compound failure. Watch the distinction between a vehicle reaching somewhere and a sensing station staying covered.</p><blockquote class=\"lab-hypothesis\">Who repairs the sensing constellation when the sea breaks the plan?</blockquote></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">02 / The mechanism</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>What the little world actually does.</h2><p>Vehicles have inertia, limited turning and thrust, finite modeled battery energy and noisy localization. Reports expire and travel through a byte-limited acoustic mesh. Mother commands use that same transport. Provisioned stations, local vacancy repair and bounded assistance all begin with the same fleet and station map.</p><p>The surface and depth layers are a 3D illustration of reduced-order horizontal dynamics. Currents and transport constraints are real parts of this model, but coefficients are synthetic. No ocean trial, engineering certification or hardware interface is implied.</p><p lang=\"zh-Hans\" class=\"lab-zh\">母舰投放环境传感器，子节点面对洋流、惯性、转向限制、定位噪声和有限电量。声学消息有带宽、丢包与延迟，母舰命令也不能绕过这些限制。三维深度是示意，物理参数尚未以真实海试校准。</p></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section\"><p class=\"tiny\">03 / Recorded evidence</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Keep the inconvenient outcomes.</h2><p><strong>Local repair helped after ordinary child loss: station uptime rose from 77.24% to 80.70%, a paired mean gain of 3.47 percentage points (95% interval 2.33–4.63). Under compound failure, it fell behind provisioned stations: 75.65% versus 77.15%. Bounded mother assistance added almost no average gain.</strong></p><p>Local repair can recover empty stations after node loss; delayed reports, congestion and partial views can also make repair worse. Mothership help must arrive over a real simulated link.</p><p class=\"small\">Paired seeded simulations. Every retained result can be regenerated from the versioned source; these are synthetic experiments, not field validation.</p><details class=\"lab-batch\"><summary>Inspect every world and treatment</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\"><table><caption class=\"tiny\">Station uptime · mean by predeclared world</caption><thead><tr><th>World / treatment</th><th>Mean %</th><th>n</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope=\"row\">An ordinary deployment / Provisioned stations</th><td>83.89</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">An ordinary deployment / Local repair</th><td>83.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">An ordinary deployment / Bounded assistance</th><td>83.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Silent children / Provisioned stations</th><td>77.24</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Silent children / Local repair</th><td>80.7</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Silent children / Bounded assistance</th><td>80.73</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The silent ocean / Provisioned stations</th><td>83.89</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The silent ocean / Local repair</th><td>83.32</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">The silent ocean / Bounded assistance</th><td>83.31</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Mother goes dark / Provisioned stations</th><td>83.89</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Mother goes dark / Local repair</th><td>83.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Mother goes dark / Bounded assistance</th><td>83.88</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">A moving world / Provisioned stations</th><td>83.75</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">A moving world / Local repair</th><td>83.75</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">A moving world / Bounded assistance</th><td>83.75</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Three blows at once / Provisioned stations</th><td>77.15</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Three blows at once / Local repair</th><td>75.65</td><td>24</td></tr><tr><th scope=\"row\">Three blows at once / Bounded assistance</th><td>75.65</td><td>24</td></tr></tbody></table></div></details><p class=\"small\">One chosen seed is an illustration. The downloadable batch retains every world and treatment; null means unavailable. A confidence interval describes the sampled synthetic worlds, not the real world.</p><div class=\"lab-links\"><a href=\"/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/results.json\" download>All recorded runs ↓</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/README.md\">Method &amp; reproduction</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/model.mjs\">Read the model</a><a href=\"/agent-swarm/ocean-swarm/source.zip\" download>Source package ↓</a></div></div></section>\n <section class=\"lab-section lab-method\"><p class=\"tiny\">04 / Inspect the boundary</p><div class=\"lab-prose\"><h2>Enough detail to disagree.</h2><details><summary>Inputs, budgets and observation boundaries</summary><dl data-audit></dl></details><details><summary>Every measure in the current run</summary><div class=\"lab-table-scroll\" data-summary></div></details><ul><li>Synthetic horizontal dynamics; the 3D depth is illustrative, not a hydrodynamic simulation.</li><li>The station map is provisioned to everyone. Actual coverage and remote survival are evaluator-only.</li><li>Modeled energy and acoustic transport expose tradeoffs; their coefficients are not calibrated to hardware.</li><li>Population sweeps increase total initial payload and energy. Arm comparisons at one population have equal budgets.</li></ul><p class=\"small\">3D sketching adds depth to the explanation. It does not add an unmodeled physical dimension, extra sensor data or unearned intelligence to the experiment.</p></div></section><nav class=\"lab-next\"><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/asteroid-button/\">← The Asteroid Button</a><a href=\"/intelligence/agent-swarm/minimum-intelligence/\">Minimum Intelligence →</a></nav></div>";
---
<BaseLayout title="Ocean Swarm — Agent Swarm Lab — Robin Xie" {path} {description} {schema}>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/agent-swarm/lab.css"/>
<Fragment set:html={content}/>
<script is:inline type="module" src="/agent-swarm/client.mjs"></script>
</BaseLayout>
